WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.103 --> 00:00:03.114
- I never had the grand intention

00:00:03.114 --> 00:00:04.618
that I wanted to be an accordion

00:00:04.618 --> 00:00:05.916
store owner when I grew up.

00:00:05.916 --> 00:00:08.034
I had seen accordions before,

00:00:08.034 --> 00:00:10.639
but until I actually picked one up,

00:00:10.639 --> 00:00:11.822
and played the notes,

00:00:11.822 --> 00:00:13.211
and moved the bellows,

00:00:13.211 --> 00:00:16.036
I just, it was one of those moments where,

00:00:16.036 --> 00:00:17.720
where has this been all my life?

00:00:17.720 --> 00:00:20.483
(accordion music)

00:00:20.483 --> 00:00:22.500
I am the owner of one of the largest

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:24.208
accordion shops in the world.

00:00:24.208 --> 00:00:27.041
(accordion music)

00:00:30.558 --> 00:00:32.110
I started with the accordion when

00:00:32.110 --> 00:00:33.994
I was about to head off to college.

00:00:33.994 --> 00:00:35.262
I was trying to figure out how

00:00:35.262 --> 00:00:36.662
I was going to play piano there,

00:00:36.662 --> 00:00:39.793
and I remembered that
my dad played accordion.

00:00:39.793 --> 00:00:42.339
It's really great to get to know my dad

00:00:42.339 --> 00:00:44.347
through something that he really liked,

00:00:44.347 --> 00:00:46.168
and something that was important to him,

00:00:46.168 --> 00:00:47.216
which was music.

00:00:47.216 --> 00:00:49.892
He unfortunately died
when I was five years old,

00:00:49.892 --> 00:00:52.492
so I really didn't know him very well.

00:00:52.492 --> 00:00:54.714
You know, the ability to connect,

00:00:54.714 --> 00:00:56.016
I think it's something that

00:00:56.016 --> 00:00:58.674
I always wish I had with my dad,

00:00:58.674 --> 00:01:02.627
but, you know, I look
forward to having with Reed.

00:01:02.627 --> 00:01:05.877
(playing Jingle Bells)

00:01:07.181 --> 00:01:11.443
My son started on a toy
accordion at age two.

00:01:11.443 --> 00:01:13.804
I think if he's anything like me or my dad

00:01:13.804 --> 00:01:15.383
then he'll like music,

00:01:15.383 --> 00:01:16.806
and it's perfectly fine with me

00:01:16.806 --> 00:01:19.864
if he plays another instrument.

00:01:19.864 --> 00:01:22.498
I just want to ultimately
be able to connect with him

00:01:22.498 --> 00:01:25.429
and it's a great experience
to express yourself

00:01:25.429 --> 00:01:27.846
through a musical instrument.

00:01:28.716 --> 00:01:30.579
I think this one's really a great sound

00:01:30.579 --> 00:01:32.679
for like a tango music.

00:01:32.679 --> 00:01:34.077
Possibly could also pass this

00:01:34.077 --> 00:01:36.433
as Count Dracula's private accordion.

00:01:36.433 --> 00:01:38.202
I sometimes use that in combination

00:01:38.202 --> 00:01:42.369
(laughing) with my Dracula fang costume.

00:01:43.258 --> 00:01:46.443
Probably should cut that part.

00:01:46.443 --> 00:01:47.964
In the U.S., there's very few people

00:01:47.964 --> 00:01:51.123
that know a lot about accordions
and that can repair them.

00:01:51.123 --> 00:01:54.081
Many of the people that had that knowledge

00:01:54.081 --> 00:01:57.184
were retiring and really not interested

00:01:57.184 --> 00:01:59.696
in expanding out to the internet.

00:01:59.696 --> 00:02:02.406
We started in my apartment,

00:02:02.406 --> 00:02:04.242
ya know, just listing things on eBay.

00:02:04.242 --> 00:02:06.969
And we realized it was
a great business model.

00:02:06.969 --> 00:02:09.040
It's amazing to just
type in a few key words

00:02:09.040 --> 00:02:13.207
and see new and used accordions
from all over the world.

00:02:15.165 --> 00:02:16.964
Reed is growing up in an environment

00:02:16.964 --> 00:02:18.857
where he sees accordions all the time,

00:02:18.857 --> 00:02:21.397
so naturally he thinks
that a lot of people

00:02:21.397 --> 00:02:22.488
play the accordion.

00:02:22.488 --> 00:02:24.068
And he gets to see me perform,

00:02:24.068 --> 00:02:26.580
he gets to see my band
Polkadelphia perform.

00:02:26.580 --> 00:02:28.341
- Three, two, one,

00:02:28.341 --> 00:02:30.841
(polka music)

00:02:32.501 --> 00:02:36.451
♫ There's a store in Philly
where accordion is king.

00:02:36.451 --> 00:02:39.871
♫ We only sell one thing,
so hear our bellows ring ♫

00:02:39.871 --> 00:02:42.529
- I'm looking forward to
connecting with my son

00:02:42.529 --> 00:02:45.120
in the same way that I often wished

00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:48.703
my dad had the opportunity
to work with me.

00:02:50.362 --> 00:02:51.675
The most important thing for me

00:02:51.675 --> 00:02:55.361
is to instill that sense of
finding what he really likes

00:02:55.361 --> 00:02:57.325
and something that he'll wake up each day

00:02:57.325 --> 00:02:58.795
and be excited about.

00:02:58.795 --> 00:03:01.906
♫ Liberty Bellows, Liberty Bellows,

00:03:01.906 --> 00:03:06.073
♫ The one stop squeezebox shop ♫

